<p>I just noticed that this SCP was posted maybe minutes before I opened it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;I'm&nbsp;going&nbsp;to&nbsp;try&nbsp;to&nbsp;put&nbsp;together&nbsp;some&nbsp;details.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Probably&nbsp;not&nbsp;even&nbsp;close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So there is a thing that happens to worlds that have achieved unity, but the thing isn't caused by the planet achieving unity, it's caused by the Observer Effect. In other words, another world observing the first.</p>
<p>Upon being observed, the world &#8230; ?</p>
<p>Other details.</p>
<p>There's a pattern screamer here. This is what caused the drone to freak out. Like all paterm screamers, it continues to take the shape of whatever the observer expects to see until focus is broken.</p>
<p>There also seems to be references to several canons like McTriss, Rat's Nest, and I think I saw a reference to the invisible lizard from Bellerverse. Interesting thing is that those canons conflict, which says to me that post-3426 worlds are actually Earth from different canons.</p>
<p>Put it together&#8230; you have a pattern screamer that reflects other SCP canons. This might explain the Poe reference in the comments on the suppliment. Maybe that means all of the canons can look up at the night sky and see a pattern screamer of the 3426 world.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Other than that&#8230; uh&#8230; gimme a hint.</p>

