			<div class="content" id="post-content-3821862">
									

<p>Yeah, I immediately recognized that whatever is happening to post-3426 world's looked just like that. However, I think the 3426 prime world is safe so long as it has its own SCP-3930.</p>
<p>Pattern screamers require attention to grow in power, which means any world that has a 3930 is restricting knowledge of 3930 by virtue of its containment protocols.</p>
<p>Any world that has been consumed by a pattern screamer would be ones where Anomaly 3930 was never discovered.</p>
<p>My theory is that these post-3426 worlds all had legends of their own 3930. When they achieved unity, urban legends of the 3930 anomaly got uploaded to the cloud. Some worlds immediately succumbed to the 3930 Anomaly, as everyone became aware of it at the same time. Those that didn't managed to hold on until anothe world looked into the night sky and observed their world, causing the pattern screamer to explode in size. This is why some world's didn't experience a 3426 event until after they were discovered by the foundation of 3426 prime.</p>
<p>None of this is incompatible with the theory that these are the worlds of the other canons. In fact, one can read the Rat's nest canon as a modified pattern screamer, though it is a bit of a stretch.</p>

