														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4207044">
									

<p>I'll be honest: maybe I'm jaded, but the &quot;civilization vanishes as soon as it achieves utopia&quot; premise I found kinda lukewarm, going in.</p>
<p>The excellence here comes by virtue of how it ties into the existing &quot;canon&quot; involving Pattern Screamers. It's a wonderfully vicious, no-holds-barred apocalyptic companion piece to the subtle creep of 3930. It doesn't need to stand on it's own because it exists to up the stakes. And it does so brilliantly.</p>
<p>I love this flavor of existential horror that so deftly casts nonexistence as something less of a concept and more of a <em>character</em>, and never going too hammy about it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
